{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_336b6f28a274f3688e71bd905515ed23c7d92fbde45a6b450024141b4e88f535"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each agent gets companion terminal shells in the same worktree, and multiple companion terminals per agent are supported."},{"claim_ids":["clm_47c97e0b1ae495ff5fae8d6fddbe51100710e2bb64f6f148d2c16c25253a876b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Projects support a startup command run in the new worktree before the provider launches, with env expansion, DUX_* environment variables, and log/rerun palette commands; failure does not block agent creation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6af25d1b0d573d5832195e4efa762443efcd4a1ab5def7154d4b4ce7cb011643"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The right pane provides git staging: stage/unstage files, view syntax-highlighted diffs, write commit messages, push, and pull; AI commit-message drafting uses the provider in oneshot mode with a customizable prompt."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7375a5afe5e3c460771b3fd74b0e571b033b13bcffc2a523fb5097cd4ac5d9db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session state persists in sessions.sqlite3 alongside the config, and logs go to dux.log in the config directory with a configurable level and path."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8903dc642be7c1c55d384f35fbb379ec12ab08b4c5a489043a6c6d57eac34944"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Palette commands include change-agent-provider, change-default-provider, and change-project-default-provider for switching providers per worktree, globally, or per project, with resume_args reused when available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a22d9d059994befb9bce672d8aab79cd9c3d58b8102df4511c9842432f8d5b94"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Any terminal command can be a provider via a TOML config entry with command, args, and optional resume_args; built-in defaults include Claude, Codex, and OpenCode, and adding a provider is config-only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b4f5c8f8286acf5097cd8a57f0be616fb4772c5b20bdd7f7fcac386485332d4b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Themes use the Opaline TOML format; custom themes live next to the config file, resolution prefers user themes then bundled dux_dark then built-in Opaline themes, falling back to dux_dark with a logged warning."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df90e48dec2785e69ad94e41d095d61cdc775973453854792fae20c2fd5d66ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"dux is a terminal UI that runs multiple AI coding agents side by side, each in its own git worktree, with companion terminals, macros, commit generation, and a command palette."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f90c6ce639f60c5dd3541de2e4ee89d90a6a0a0ee12c1c17ab004db824b8c024"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents run through a PTY like a normal shell, so CLIs such as Claude, Codex, or OpenCode behave as they would in a regular terminal, including MCP servers, hooks, and permission dialogs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa614dff30db6eb0c77c1e534ebd5c1ff3e47f09dfcf21dccfbcbe2f8f1fd41e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"git is required on PATH; the gh CLI is optional and enables PR status tracking shown as status pills in the interface."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ff104f5610089b2d526b76c26b365dd298cdceffa6c8e9027d34ce441cfb190d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The interface has three panes: projects and agent sessions on the left, the agent's live terminal output or diff in the center, and changed files, staging, and diffs on the right."}],"claim_ids":["clm_336b6f28a274f3688e71bd905515ed23c7d92fbde45a6b450024141b4e88f535","clm_47c97e0b1ae495ff5fae8d6fddbe51100710e2bb64f6f148d2c16c25253a876b","clm_6af25d1b0d573d5832195e4efa762443efcd4a1ab5def7154d4b4ce7cb011643","clm_7375a5afe5e3c460771b3fd74b0e571b033b13bcffc2a523fb5097cd4ac5d9db","clm_8903dc642be7c1c55d384f35fbb379ec12ab08b4c5a489043a6c6d57eac34944","clm_a22d9d059994befb9bce672d8aab79cd9c3d58b8102df4511c9842432f8d5b94","clm_b4f5c8f8286acf5097cd8a57f0be616fb4772c5b20bdd7f7fcac386485332d4b","clm_df90e48dec2785e69ad94e41d095d61cdc775973453854792fae20c2fd5d66ec","clm_f90c6ce639f60c5dd3541de2e4ee89d90a6a0a0ee12c1c17ab004db824b8c024","clm_fa614dff30db6eb0c77c1e534ebd5c1ff3e47f09dfcf21dccfbcbe2f8f1fd41e","clm_ff104f5610089b2d526b76c26b365dd298cdceffa6c8e9027d34ce441cfb190d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_cbfe3869314a491a8ba9d5b0e6b29aba","id":"pg_5a2f9b6ad3115f389055f08bc8a68281","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/patrickdappollonio-dux-readme-md-14e044d616d2-f08bc8a68281.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1a20a257cf9e59208174d271dbe9b397"],"title":"patrickdappollonio/dux/README.md @ 14e044d616d2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cbfe3869314a491a8ba9d5b0e6b29aba"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_19c20ba1c908846385fa0b12122781533e156a23300f497c9bb8a046300a45bf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors verify changes with cargo fmt, cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings (a CI gate on every PR), and cargo test, and every change should include unit tests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_566f79842b0096c0e360c3a6e5a49fc17ac9911db93c1d27b585f4916483cb45"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the src/app/ TUI is split into focused submodules (mod.rs, input.rs, render.rs, sessions.rs, workers.rs), and changes should stay scoped to the relevant submodule."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7375a5afe5e3c460771b3fd74b0e571b033b13bcffc2a523fb5097cd4ac5d9db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session state persists in sessions.sqlite3 alongside the config, and logs go to dux.log in the config directory with a configurable level and path."}],"claim_ids":["clm_19c20ba1c908846385fa0b12122781533e156a23300f497c9bb8a046300a45bf","clm_566f79842b0096c0e360c3a6e5a49fc17ac9911db93c1d27b585f4916483cb45","clm_7375a5afe5e3c460771b3fd74b0e571b033b13bcffc2a523fb5097cd4ac5d9db"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_cbfe3869314a491a8ba9d5b0e6b29aba","id":"pg_9c93c21222f55f01a16f92da97a3af30","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/patrickdappollonio-dux-claude-md-14e044d616d2-92da97a3af30.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_fbc4e6918b155fc1ad9b2ebbf18cdfb8"],"title":"patrickdappollonio/dux/CLAUDE.md @ 14e044d616d2","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cbfe3869314a491a8ba9d5b0e6b29aba"}
